_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nThe documentation for adding providers to a REST client using the `quarkus.rest-client.\"client\".providers` configuration property states that it should specify a map:\nhttps://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/3554bbc4c167f666220ca5d2abddad719fe57319/extensions/resteasy-classic/rest-client-config/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/restclient/config/RestClientsConfig.java#L179-L185\n\nThis does not appear to be the case any longer. Instead, it's just a simple list of class names:\nhttps://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/3554bbc4c167f666220ca5d2abddad719fe57319/extensions/resteasy-classic/resteasy-client/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/restclient/runtime/RestClientBase.java#L262-L266\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe documentation states that the `quarkus.rest-client.\"client\".providers` configuration property specifies a string list of class names to register as providers for the client.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe documentation incorrectly claims that the configuration property specifies a \"class name\" → \"priority\" map.\n\n### How to Reproduce?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Output of `uname -a` or `ver`\n\n_No response_\n\n### Output of `java -version`\n\n_No response_\n\n### Quarkus version or git rev\n\n3.17.4\n\n### Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"geoand","id":4374975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNzQ5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4374975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand","html_url":"https://github.com/geoand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"h